WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:08.400
Phase zero: Collecting Humans Before You Have Anything to Offer Them On Wishonia, if someone discovered everyone was dying

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.880
from preventable causes, they would simply stop dying from preventable causes.

3
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:21.100
On Earth, you need a tax-exempt entity, a bank account, and written permission from something called the Securities and

4
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:28.860
Exchange Commission before you're allowed to try. The Securities and Exchange Commission regulates securities, which are

5
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.340
financial instruments, not the kind of security where people stop dying.

6
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.940
That would be a different department. You don't have that department.

7
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:45.660
So you can't accept money yet. You can't sell bonds yet. You can't do anything that involves the movement of small pieces

8
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:55.060
of paper. What you CAN do is collect names. The goal of Phase zero is building a database of every human who agrees that

9
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.080
dying from preventable causes is a strange thing to tolerate.

10
00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:07.320
It's a Kickstarter where the reward tier is "possibly not dying," which is the most compelling crowdfunding offer in history,

11
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:13.870
and yet somehow requires marketing. The Bureaucratic Nesting Doll Problem.

12
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.960
On your planet, before you can accept donations, you need five oh one c three status.

13
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:25.840
Before you can sell bonds, you need S.E.C. registration. Before you can do either, you need a bank account.

14
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.430
Before you can open a bank account, you need an organization.

15
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.580
Before you can have an organization, you need the bank account.

16
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.620
It's like a door that requires a key that's locked inside the room the door opens to.

17
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:47.560
Your species built this system on purpose. The solution is the same one humans have used every time this has happened, which

18
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:55.420
is every time. You collect people first, then point at the crowd when the institutions ask "but who wants this?".

19
00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.640
Abolition started with a list of names. Suffrage started with a list of names.

20
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.380
Civil rights started with a list of names. Someone wrote down who agreed.

21
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.360
The names became a number. The number became bargaining power.

22
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:17.400
The bargaining power became policy. Then the policy became a holiday, and everyone pretended they'd agreed all along.

23
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.820
Your species does this every forty years and never recognizes the pattern.

24
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:31.040
Three Types of Humans Who Want to Help. People who agree with "dying is bad" fall into three categories, sorted by which

25
00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.930
part of their brain activates first. Spreadsheet Humans (Investors).

26
00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:44.180
These are humans who hear "two hundred and seventy-two percent annual return backed by redirected military spending" and

27
00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.220
immediately open a spreadsheet. Their pupils dilate. Their pulse quickens.

28
00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.920
They ask about the term structure. Then they ask about the term structure again.

29
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.000
Then they ask a third question, which is also about the term structure.

30
00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:03.180
These humans are not broken. They are simply running financial software on moral hardware.

31
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:10.220
They process "millions of people are dying" faster when it arrives formatted as a revenue projection.

32
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.780
They'll wait years for a good investment to materialize. They will not wait thirty seconds for a bad one.

33
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:24.260
If your math is solid, these humans will follow you to the gates of hell, provided the risk-adjusted return on entering

34
00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.940
hell is competitive. Do not try to make them cry. Make them calculate.

35
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.200
Crying is temporary. Compound interest is forever. Heart Humans (Advocates).

36
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:44.840
These are humans motivated by the mission itself. They share things on social media, write letters to politicians, volunteer

37
00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:50.040
time, donate money they probably shouldn't, and cry at commercials about dogs.

38
00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:55.280
They are, frankly, the only reason your species has ever improved anything.

39
00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.240
Without them, the spreadsheet humans would still be optimizing returns on the slave trade.

40
00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:08.780
The critical mistake every movement makes with these humans is telling them to "care about this" without giving them something

41
00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:16.899
to do. I have watched four thousand, two hundred and ninety-seven years of humans being told to "raise awareness."

42
00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.480
The awareness has been raised. It's been raised so many times it has a penthouse suite.

43
00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:29.160
The awareness is just sitting there, fully raised, doing nothing, because nobody told it what to do next.

44
00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.500
Give heart humans a button. Give them a form. Give them a link to share.

45
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.280
Give them a specific politician to call and a specific sentence to say when they call.

46
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.930
If you give a human a feeling without an action, you haven't recruited a supporter.

47
00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:50.230
You've manufactured a sad person. Your planet has enough of those.

48
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:59.980
Institutional Humans (Partners). Organizations (nonprofits, research institutions, health agencies) that already work on

49
00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.540
pieces of this problem. They have infrastructure, credibility, and mailing lists.

50
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.740
You have a framework that could make their existing work more effective.

51
00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:16.940
This is a trade, not charity. Approach it like one. Nobody wants to be "partnered with" by someone who clearly just wants

52
00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:23.180
their mailing list. They can tell. Humans are surprisingly good at detecting when other humans want their mailing list.

53
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:31.280
It's one of their few reliable instincts. What you're offering is real: a funding mechanism that could multiply their impact

54
00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:39.500
without requiring them to write another grant application. (Grant applications are documents in which humans spend two hundred

55
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:45.060
hours explaining why they deserve money, so that a committee can spend forty minutes deciding they don't.

56
00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:54.580
It's your species' least efficient art form.). One warning: institutions are territorial in the way that dogs are territorial,

57
00:05:54.980 --> 00:06:01.940
except dogs eventually stop barking. Two nonprofits working on the same disease will fight each other harder than they fight

58
00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:09.920
the disease. This is called "the nonprofit sector." Approach each one as if they are the only organization doing this work.

59
00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.120
They already believe this, so you're just agreeing with them.

60
00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:21.220
Phase Zero: The Shopping List. By the end of Phase zero, you want: one hundred thousand plus registered humans who typed

61
00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:27.500
their name into a box indicating they prefer living. This sounds like it should be everyone, but on your planet, "dying

62
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.740
is bad" is apparently a niche political position that requires organized support.

63
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:39.080
one thousand plus spreadsheet humans with stated investment ranges (how many papers they'd give you, if you were allowed

64
00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.070
to accept papers, which you're not yet, but you're writing it down for later).

65
00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:51.500
one hundred plus institutional humans with expressed interest in collaborating (or at least not actively opposing you, which

66
00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:59.880
on your planet counts as enthusiasm). one billion dollars plus in stated investment demand (registered, not committed; this

67
00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:06.540
is humans saying "I would give you this many papers" without actually giving you the papers, which your species calls a

68
00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:14.060
"letter of intent" and treats as meaningful). This database is your ammunition for every bureaucratic nesting doll that

69
00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:20.500
follows. When you apply for five oh one c three status, you point at the list and say "here are our supporters."

70
00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.540
When you file S.E.C. registration, you point at the list and say "here is market demand."

71
00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.290
When you meet politicians, you point at the list and say "here are your constituents."

72
00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.740
When you launch, you point at the list and say "here are your users.".

73
00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:42.020
Bureaucrats don't respond to arguments. They respond to evidence that other people already responded to arguments.

74
00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:48.340
No bureaucrat in the history of your civilization has ever said "this is a good idea, let's do it."

75
00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.400
They say "how many people already think this is a good idea?"

76
00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.600
and then, if the number is large enough, they act as though they thought of it themselves.

77
00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:04.760
Your entire civilization runs on this principle, and nobody admits it because admitting it would require a committee to

78
00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:08.660
approve the admission. Getting Started (It Takes Twenty Minutes).

79
00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:13.500
Build three boxes where humans type their name to indicate they prefer living.

80
00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:18.090
One box for spreadsheet humans (asks: how many papers would you invest?).

81
00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:22.700
One box for heart humans (asks: what skills do you have? how many hours per week?).

82
00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:27.460
One box for institutional humans (asks: what does your organization do?

83
00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.340
how many people does it reach?). This takes twenty minutes.

84
00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:36.820
Your species spent longer than that choosing the name "Department of Defense" for a department that mainly attacks people.

85
00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:42.380
Put up a website. The three boxes and the argument. It does not need to be pretty.

86
00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.840
No movement in history was stopped because the font was wrong.

87
00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.740
The suffragettes did not fail to get the vote because their pamphlets used Comic Sans.

88
00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.280
(Comic Sans didn't exist yet, which is the only reason they didn't.

89
00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:57.180
Your species would absolutely have used Comic Sans on suffrage pamphlets.).

90
00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:04.180
Three. Start telling other humans. Social media, Reddit, forums, conferences, your dentist.

91
00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.160
Especially your dentist. You're already trapped in the chair.

92
00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:13.380
They can't leave either. Their hands are in your mouth. It's the most captive audience in human civilization.

93
00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:19.920
You're not going to get a better recruiting environment than a room where both parties are contractually obligated to remain

94
00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.040
in close proximity and one of them is holding sharp instruments.

95
00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:31.940
Four. Send monthly updates with real numbers. "Three thousand two hundred and forty-seven registered investors representing

96
00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:38.060
one hundred and eighty million dollars in stated investment demand" beats "the movement is growing!"

97
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:44.540
in the same way that "your tumor is two point three centimeters" beats "your health situation is evolving."

98
00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:51.640
Adults prefer arithmetic to enthusiasm. Enthusiasm is what humans feel before they do math.

99
00:09:52.300 --> 00:10:00.200
Arithmetic is what humans feel after. Both are useful. But only one of them convinces spreadsheet humans, and you need the

100
00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:06.250
spreadsheet humans because they have the papers. The Comforting Asymmetry.

101
00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:14.560
The military-industrial complex has a sixty-five-year head start, unlimited budgets, and thousands of professional persuaders.

102
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:19.860
You have a spreadsheet and an argument. Historically, that's been enough.

103
00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:27.200
Every major social change in your species' history was started by someone with less money, fewer connections, and worse

104
00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:34.460
odds than the thing they were trying to change. Abolitionists were outspent by slave owners by a factor your calculators

105
00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:41.900
would refuse to display. Suffragettes were outspent by the entire concept of patriarchy, which didn't even need a budget

106
00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:48.940
because it was just how things were. Civil rights activists were outspent by the governments actively trying to kill them.

107
00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:56.800
They all had the same thing you have: an argument that was obviously correct, and enough humans willing to write their names

108
00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:04.180
down. It shouldn't work this way. Spreadsheets, budgets, and lobbyists should always beat arguments and names.

109
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:12.180
But your species is weird like that. You're the only civilization I've observed where being right occasionally defeats being

110
00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:18.420
rich. It happens rarely, and it takes too long, and it requires an embarrassing amount of suffering first.

111
00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:22.390
But it happens. And it starts with a list of names.
